	<xsl:template match="/" name="AAA04F007">			
		
				
				     <fo:block>
				<xsl:call-template name="CommonHeader" />
			</fo:block>
			
		      <fo:block margin-top="12mm"/>
		     <fo:block text-align="center" font-weight="bold" font-size="10px">BROAD ADVANTAGE ENDORSEMENT</fo:block>
		    
		     <fo:block margin-top="10mm"/>
		<fo:block font-family="Arial Narrow, 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, sans-serif;" font-size="10px" text-align="justify">
			<fo:block space-after="4mm">
				In consideration of the premium charged, it is agreed that:
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
			<fo:list-block>
			<fo:list-item space-after="4mm">
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				1.		
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="7mm">
			<fo:block space-after="4mm">
				Item 7. of the Declarations, Optional Extended Reporting Period, is deleted in its entirety and replaced with the following:
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block space-after="4mm">
			<fo:table>
			<fo:table-column column-width="30mm"/>
			<fo:table-column column-width="150mm"/>
			<fo:table-body>
			<fo:table-row>
			<fo:table-cell padding-left="2mm" border="1pt solid black" padding-top="2mm">
			<fo:block>
				Item 7.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:table-cell>
			<fo:table-cell border="1pt solid black">
			<fo:block>
			<fo:table>
			<fo:table-column column-width="50mm"/>
			<fo:table-column column-width="60mm"/>
			<fo:table-body>
			<fo:table-row>
			<fo:table-cell number-columns-spanned="2" padding-top="2mm">
			<fo:block>
				<fo:inline font-weight="bold">Optional Extended Reporting Period:</fo:inline>
			</fo:block>
			</fo:table-cell>
			</fo:table-row>
			<fo:table-row>
			<fo:table-cell padding-top="2mm">
			<fo:block>
			<fo:list-block>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				(a)
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="14mm">
			<fo:block>
				Length of Time
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				12 months
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				36 months
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				60 months
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				72 months
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			</fo:list-block>
			</fo:block>
			</fo:table-cell>
			<fo:table-cell padding-top="2mm">
			<fo:block>
			<fo:list-block>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				(b)
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="14mm">
			<fo:block>
				Additional Premium
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				100% of the annual premium
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				185% of the annual premium
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				225% of the annual premium
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				250% of the annual premium
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			</fo:list-block>
			</fo:block>
			</fo:table-cell>
			</fo:table-row>
			</fo:table-body>
			</fo:table>
			</fo:block>
			</fo:table-cell>
			</fo:table-row>
			</fo:table-body>
			</fo:table>
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				If any of the above lengths or premium charges conflict with a state
				amendatory endorsement attached to this policy, the terms providing the
				broadest coverage insurable under applicable law shall prevail.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item space-after="4mm">
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				2.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="7mm">
			<fo:block space-after="4mm">
				Section III., Extension D., Extended Reporting Period Extensions,
				subsection 3., <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Retired Insured</fo:inline> Extended Reporting Period, is amended by
				addition of the following:
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				The additional premium charges stated herein shall be waived for a
				<fo:inline font-weight="bold">Retired Insured</fo:inline> who has been insured for his/her <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Professional Services</fo:inline>
				by the <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Insurer</fo:inline> for three consecutive years prior to the date the
				<fo:inline font-weight="bold">Insured</fo:inline> becomes a <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Retired Insured</fo:inline>, and such <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Retired Insured</fo:inline>:
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block space-after="4mm">
			<fo:list-block>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				(a)
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="14mm">
			<fo:block>
				was, and is, the sole practitioner accountant insured during said three consecutive years; and
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				(b)
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="14mm">
			<fo:block>
				is the sole practitioner accountant during the <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Policy Period</fo:inline> shown in Item 2. of the Declarations.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			</fo:list-block>
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				For the purpose of the applicability of this waiver of additional
				premium, “sole practitioner accountant” means one who was engaged in
				performing <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Professional Services</fo:inline> alone, with no other partners,
				accountants, consultants, bookkeepers or other professional working on
				client engagements.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item space-after="4mm">
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				3.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="7mm">
			<fo:block space-after="4mm">
				Section III., Extension D., Extended Reporting Period Extensions, is amended by addition of the following:
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
			<fo:list-block>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block font-weight="bold">
				•
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="14mm">
			<fo:block font-weight="bold" space-after="4mm">
				Death or Disability Extended Reporting Period
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
			<fo:list-block>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				(a)
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="21mm">
			<fo:block>
				If an <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Insured</fo:inline> dies (except by suicide) or becomes <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Totally and
				Permanently Disabled</fo:inline> during the <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Policy Period</fo:inline>, such <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Insured</fo:inline> shall have
				the right to an unlimited period of time during which <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Claims</fo:inline> may be
				reported to the <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Insurer</fo:inline> pursuant to Section VI., General Condition A.,
				Notice of <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Claim</fo:inline> or Circumstance, paragraph 1. Coverage under any such
				extension of time to report a <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Claim</fo:inline> (referred to below as the Death or
				Disability Extended Reporting Period) shall apply solely to negligent
				acts, errors or omissions in rendering <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Professional Services</fo:inline>:
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block space-after="4mm">
			<fo:list-block>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				(1)
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="28mm">
			<fo:block>
				committed or attempted prior to the date of such <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Insured’s</fo:inline> death or total and permanent disability; and
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				(2)
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="28mm">
			<fo:block>
				which are not otherwise excluded by any terms, conditions or exclusions of this policy.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			</fo:list-block>
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				The Death or Disability Extended Reporting Period will apply only to
				such <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Insured</fo:inline> as an individual accountant and will not apply to any
				other accountant, including but not limited to any accountant acting as
				an independent contractor or contracting on a per diem basis.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			</fo:list-block>
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			</fo:list-block>
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			</fo:list-block>
			</fo:block>
			
	      <fo:block margin-top="25mm"/>
			<fo:block  font-size="10px" color="grey" text-align="left">ISMIE AAA-04-F007 (04012022)
	       	 <fo:block margin-top="-0.5cm" font-size="10px" color="grey" text-align="right">Page 1 of 4</fo:block>
	       	 </fo:block>
			<fo:block break-after="page"></fo:block>
			<fo:block text-align="center" color="grey" font-size="12px">THIS ENDORSEMENT CHANGES THE POLICY, Please READ IT CAREFULLY.</fo:block>
			<fo:block margin-top="10mm"/>  
			<fo:block>
			<fo:list-block>
			<fo:list-item space-after="4mm">
			<fo:list-item-label start-indent="21mm">
			<fo:block>
				(b)
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="28mm">
			<fo:block>
				Any specific Death or Disability Extended Reporting Period must be
				elected by the <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Named Insured</fo:inline> within 60 days of the expiration date of
				the <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Policy Period</fo:inline>. No additional premium will be charged. The
				Deductible amount and Deductible provisions of this policy do not apply
				to <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Claims</fo:inline> first made against such individual accountant <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Insured</fo:inline> during
				any Death or Disability Extended Reporting Period.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item space-after="4mm">
			<fo:list-item-label start-indent="21mm">
			<fo:block>
				(c)
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="28mm">
			<fo:block>
				The <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Insurer’s</fo:inline> Limit of Liability for all <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Claims</fo:inline> first made against
				an <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Insured</fo:inline> during any Death or Disability Extended Reporting Period
				will be part of, and not in addition to, the Limit of Liability shown
				in Item 3. of the Declarations, regardless of the number of Death or
				Disability Extended Reporting Periods elected.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item space-after="4mm">
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				4.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="7mm">
			<fo:block space-after="4mm">
				Section III., Extension F., Defendant Reimbursement Extension, is amended by addition of the following:
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				Any payments made regarding such attendance will be in addition to the Limit of Liability and are not subject to the Deductible.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item space-after="4mm">
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				5.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="7mm">
			<fo:block space-after="4mm">
				Section III., Extension G., Regulatory Inquiry Extension, is deleted in its entirety and replaced with the following:
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
			<fo:list-block>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block font-weight="bold">
				G.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="14mm">
			<fo:block font-weight="bold" space-after="4mm">
				Regulatory Inquiry Extension
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				If a:
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
			<fo:list-block>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				1.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="21mm">
			<fo:block>
				regulatory body;
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				2.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="21mm">
			<fo:block>
				state licensing board;
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				3.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="21mm">
			<fo:block>
				public oversight board; or
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				4.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="21mm">
			<fo:block>
				government agency,
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			</fo:list-block>
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				having regulatory authority over the <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Insured’s Professional Services</fo:inline>,
				first initiates an investigation of any <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Insured</fo:inline> during the <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Policy
				Period</fo:inline> which arises from <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Professional Services</fo:inline> rendered on or after the
				<fo:inline font-weight="bold">Prior Acts Date</fo:inline> and, such regulatory inquiry is reported to the <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Insurer</fo:inline>
				pursuant to Section VI., General Condition A., Notice of <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Claim</fo:inline> or
				Circumstance, the <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Insurer</fo:inline> will reimburse the <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Named Insured</fo:inline> for attorney
				fees, court and regulatory body costs incurred in responding to such
				inquiry, up to $50,000. This is the maximum amount the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insurer</fo:inline> will
				reimburse, regardless of the number of such inquiries or of the number
				of <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insureds</fo:inline> involved in such inquiries, for all inquiries first
				initiated against the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insureds</fo:inline> during the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Policy Period</fo:inline> and reported to
				the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insurer</fo:inline> pursuant to Section VI., General Condition A., Notice of
				<fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Claim</fo:inline> or Circumstance. Any payments made regarding such inquiry will be
				in addition to the Limit of Liability and are not subject to the
				Deductible.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			</fo:list-block>
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item space-after="4mm">
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				6.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="7mm">
			<fo:block space-after="4mm">
				Section III., Extension H., Subpoena Assistance Extension, is amended by addition of the following:
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				Any payments made regarding such subpoena will be in addition to the Limit of Liability and are not subject to the Deductible.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item space-after="4mm">
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				7.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="7mm">
			<fo:block space-after="4mm">
				Section III., Extension I., Client Discrimination Extension, is amended by deleting the last sentence and replacing it with the following:
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				Notwithstanding anything in this policy to the contrary, any <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Defense Expenses</fo:inline> incurred regarding such allegations will be in addition to the Limit of Liability and are not subject to the Deductible.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				8.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="7mm">
			<fo:block space-after="4mm">
				Section III., Extensions, is amended by addition of the following:
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
			<fo:list-block>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block font-weight="bold">
				•
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="14mm">
			<fo:block font-weight="bold" space-after="4mm">
				Crisis Event Extension
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				The <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insurer</fo:inline> will reimburse the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Named Insured</fo:inline> up to $20,000 for <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Crisis
				Event Expenses</fo:inline> that result from a <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Crisis Event</fo:inline>&#160; first occurring and
				reported in writing to the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insurer</fo:inline> during the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Policy Period</fo:inline> pursuant to
				Section VI., General Condition A., Notice of <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Claim</fo:inline> or Circumstance. Any
				payments made regarding such event will be in addition to the Limit of
				Liability and are not subject to the Deductible.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			</fo:list-block>
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			</fo:list-block>
			</fo:block>    
	      <fo:block margin-top="35mm"/>
			<fo:block  font-size="10px" color="grey" text-align="left">ISMIE AAA-04-F007 (04012022)
	       	 <fo:block margin-top="-0.5cm" font-size="10px" color="grey" text-align="right">Page 2 of 4</fo:block>
	       	 </fo:block> 
			<fo:block break-after="page"></fo:block>
			<fo:block text-align="center" color="grey" font-size="12px">THIS ENDORSEMENT CHANGES THE POLICY, Please READ IT CAREFULLY.</fo:block>
			<fo:block margin-top="10mm"/>  
			<fo:block>
			<fo:list-block>
			<fo:list-item space-after="4mm">
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				9.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="7mm">
			<fo:block space-after="4mm">
				Section IV., Definitions, <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Insured</fo:inline>, is deleted in its entirety and replaced with the following:
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				<fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insured</fo:inline> means the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Named Insured</fo:inline>, <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Predecessor Firm</fo:inline>, and:
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
			<fo:list-block>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				(a)
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="14mm">
			<fo:block>
				any present or future principal, partner, director, officer, member or employee of the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Named Insured</fo:inline>;
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				(b)
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="14mm">
			<fo:block>
				any former principal, partner, director, officer, member or employee of
				the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Named Insured</fo:inline> or of a <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Predecessor Firm</fo:inline>;
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				(c)
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="14mm">
			<fo:block>
				the estate, heirs, executors, administrators, assigns and legal
				representatives of an <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insured</fo:inline> but only in the event of such <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insured’s</fo:inline>
				death, incapacity, insolvency or bankruptcy, and only to the extent
				that such <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insured</fo:inline> would otherwise have been provided coverage under the
				terms, conditions and exclusions of this policy; and
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				(d)
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="14mm">
			<fo:block>
				any contract or temporary employee of a <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Named Insured</fo:inline> under the direct supervision of an <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insured</fo:inline>,
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			</fo:list-block>
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				but only with respect to <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Professional Services</fo:inline> performed within the
				scope of their duties on behalf of the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Named Insured</fo:inline> or <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Predecessor
				Firm</fo:inline>.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item space-after="4mm">
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				10.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="7mm">
			<fo:block space-after="4mm">
				Section IV., Definitions, <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Predecessor Firm</fo:inline>, is deleted in its entirety and replaced with the following:
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				<fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Predecessor Firm</fo:inline> means an individual, partnership, professional
				corporation, professional association, limited liability corporation or
				partnership which was at all times engaged in <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Professional Services</fo:inline> and
				to whose financial assets and liabilities the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Named Insured</fo:inline> is the
				majority successor in interest prior to the effective date shown in
				Item 2. of the Declarations.
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				<fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Predecessor Firm</fo:inline> does not include any individual, partnership,
				professional corporation, professional association, limited liability
				corporation or partnership which was at all times engaged in
				<fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Professional Services</fo:inline> and to whose financial assets and liabilities the
				<fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Named Insured</fo:inline> becomes the majority successor in interest after the
				effective date of this policy shown in Item 2. of the Declarations
				unless the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insurer</fo:inline> at its sole discretion agrees to include such
				entity. Should the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insurer</fo:inline> agree to include such entity it may do so
				for an additional premium or with amended policy terms and conditions.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item space-after="4mm">
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				11.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="7mm">
			<fo:block space-after="4mm">
				Section IV., Definitions, is amended by addition of the following:
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
			<fo:list-block>
			<fo:list-item space-after="4mm">
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block font-weight="bold">
				•
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="14mm">
			<fo:block>
				<fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Crisis Event</fo:inline> means:
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
			<fo:list-block>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				(a)
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="21mm">
			<fo:block>
				death, departure or debilitating illness of a principal <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insured</fo:inline>;
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				(b)
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="21mm">
			<fo:block>
				dissolution of the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Named Insured</fo:inline>; or
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				(c)
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="21mm">
			<fo:block>
				incident of workplace violence;
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			</fo:list-block>
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				that the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Named Insured</fo:inline> reasonably believes will have a material adverse
				effect upon the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Named Insured’s</fo:inline> reputation.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item space-after="4mm">
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block font-weight="bold">
				•
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="14mm">
			<fo:block>
				<fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Crisis Event Expenses</fo:inline> mean reasonable fees, costs and expenses
				incurred by the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Named Insured</fo:inline> for consulting services provided by a
				public relations firm to the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Named Insured</fo:inline> in response to a <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Crisis
				Event</fo:inline>.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item space-after="4mm">
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block font-weight="bold">
				•
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="14mm">
			<fo:block>
				<fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Totally and Permanently Disabled</fo:inline> means that the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insured</fo:inline> is so disabled
				as to be wholly prevented from rendering <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Professional Services</fo:inline> provided
				that such disability:
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
			<fo:list-block>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				(a)
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="21mm">
			<fo:block>
				has existed continuously for not less than six months; and
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				(b)
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="21mm">
			<fo:block>
				is reasonably expected to be continuous and permanent.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			</fo:list-block>
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			</fo:list-block>
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				12.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="7mm">
			<fo:block space-after="4mm">
				Section V., Exclusion 1. is deleted in its entirety and replaced with the following:
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
			<fo:list-block>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				1.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="14mm">
			<fo:block>
				a dishonest, intentional, fraudulent, criminal or malicious act or
				omission or any intentional or knowing violation of law by any <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insured</fo:inline>.
				However:
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
			<fo:list-block>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				(a)
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="21mm">
			<fo:block>
				the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insurer</fo:inline> will provide the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insured</fo:inline> with a defense of such <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Claim</fo:inline>
				and pay <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Defense Expenses</fo:inline> for any such <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Claim</fo:inline> until there is a judgment,
				final adjudication or adverse admission by an <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insured</fo:inline> or a finding of
				fact against an <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insured</fo:inline> as to such conduct; and
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				(b)
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="21mm">
			<fo:block>
				this exclusion shall not apply to an <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insured</fo:inline> who, in fact, did not
				personally commit, direct or participate in committing a dishonest,
				intentional, fraudulent, criminal or malicious act or omission or any
				intentional or knowing violation of law.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			</fo:list-block>
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			</fo:list-block>
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			</fo:list-block>
			</fo:block>
	      <fo:block margin-top="35mm"/>
			<fo:block  font-size="10px" color="grey" text-align="left">ISMIE AAA-04-F007 (04012022)
	       	 <fo:block margin-top="-0.5cm" font-size="10px" color="grey" text-align="right">Page 3 of 4</fo:block>
	       	 </fo:block>
			<fo:block break-after="page"></fo:block>
			<fo:block text-align="center" color="grey" font-size="12px">THIS ENDORSEMENT CHANGES THE POLICY, Please READ IT CAREFULLY.</fo:block>
			<fo:block margin-top="10mm"/>  
			<fo:block space-after="4mm">
			<fo:list-block>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block>
				13.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="7mm">
			<fo:block space-after="4mm">
				Section VI., General Conditions, is amended by addition of the following:
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
			<fo:list-block>
			<fo:list-item>
			<fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:block font-weight="bold">
				•
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-label>
			<fo:list-item-body start-indent="14mm">
			<fo:block font-weight="bold" space-after="4mm">
				Liberalization
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block>
				If during the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Policy Period</fo:inline>, the <fo:inline font-weight="bold" font-style="italic">Insurer</fo:inline> adopts any provision that
				would broaden the coverage under this policy without an additional
				premium charge, the broadened coverage shall automatically apply to
				this policy.
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			</fo:list-block>
			</fo:block>
			</fo:list-item-body>
			</fo:list-item>
			</fo:list-block>
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block  space-after="2cm">
				All other terms, conditions and limitations of the policy remain unaltered.
			</fo:block>
			<fo:block space-after="7cm">
